WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.942
Text categories often contain small differences that create false groups.

00:00:04.942 --> 00:00:12.492
For example, Web, web, and web with extra spaces may all represent the same channel.

00:00:12.492 --> 00:00:17.727
If we do not standardize them, Pandas will treat them as separate categories.

00:00:17.727 --> 00:00:23.857
The example uses string methods to remove extra spaces and standardize capitalization.

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:27.962
Run the code and compare the value counts after cleaning.

00:00:27.962 --> 00:00:36.832
This is a useful validation step because it confirms that categories were combined the way you intended.

00:00:36.832 --> 00:00:44.952
In real datasets, you may also need to fix spelling differences or map several labels into one standard category.

00:00:44.952 --> 00:00:47.657
For example, North Carolina, NC, and N.C.

00:00:47.657 --> 00:00:51.072
may all need to become one value.

00:00:51.072 --> 00:00:54.257
The goal is not to make text look nicer.

00:00:54.257 --> 00:00:58.738
The goal is to make categories represent the same concept consistently.
